{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"48f69827-3b49-41eb-85b8-4e447ed755ab","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I consulted the `worklore` MCP server before starting, which suggested the story:\n`2026-04-24-two-cache-control-segments-so-agent-memory-writes-don-t-evic` (\"Two cache_control segments so agent memory writes don't evict the whole Claude system prompt\").\n\n### Root Cause\nPreviously, [`build_system()`](file:///private/tmp/h-JWDYlu/bot.py#L130-L138) merged `INSTRUCTIONS` and `athlete_context()` into a single text block with one `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}` marker. Because Anthropic prompt caching hashes sequentially from the prefix, any change to memory facts appended via `save_fact` modified the block and evicted the entire cached system prompt, forcing the next call to re-create cache tokens for the static instructions.\n\n### Fix Applied\nIn [`bot.py`](file:///private/tmp/h-JWDYlu/bot.py), split the system prompt into two separate segments, each marked with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`:\n1. **Static instruction block**: `INSTRUCTIONS` (invariant across users and calls).\n2. **Volatile tail**: `athlete_context(a, today)` (date, user profile, zones, goal, and facts).\n\nWhen `save_fact` writes a memory fact, only the tail block misses cache and is recreated (~240 tokens), while the static instructions block remains cached.\n\nThe explanation has been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///private/tmp/h-JWDYlu/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":72.843694,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":108175,"output_tokens":2075,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":350673,"total_tokens":110250}}}
